{"question_id": "f79", "category": "definition", "question": "What is the role of the Valuation Control Group (VCG) in the company's financial reporting?", "relevant_chunk_ids": ["udoc_fa0a9fc7a274:0776"], "reference_answer": "The Firm’s Valuation Control Group (“VCG”), which is part of the Firm’s Finance function and independent of the risk-taking functions, is responsible for verifying these estimates and determining any fair value adjustments that may be required to ensure that the Firm’s positions are recorded at fair value.", "notes": "page 169", "needs_review": true}
